On the 22nd, the director of the Environmental Supervision Bureau of the Ministry of Environmental Protection of the People's Republic of China introduced in Beijing that in August, there were a total of 57 consecutive punishment cases nationwide, and the newly revised "Environmental Protection Law" implemented at the beginning of this year significantly increased China's environmental law enforcement efforts.
At present, environmental protection organs in various parts of China can use penalties such as day-to-day continuous punishment, seizure and seizure, restriction and suspension of production and transfer to administrative detention to investigate and punish environmental crimes, and cooperate with judicial authorities to punish environmental crimes.
Zou said that in August, a total of 335 seizure and seizure cases were carried out in various parts of China; a total of 177 cases were closed and discontinued; a total of 189 cases were transferred to administrative detention, and a total of 166 cases of suspected environmental pollution crimes were transferred.
At present, China is being controlled from the end to the whole process to be embedded to comprehensively enhance environmental pollution control.
Although the downward pressure on the economy appears, China's Ministry of Environmental Protection has previously clearly stated that China should correctly deal with the positioning of environmental protection in economic development, enhance the "green concentration", the more the economic growth rate downward, the more unable to relax environmental protection and give full play to the optimization role of environmental protection in the economy.
