From the end of February to the beginning of March, from the end of February to the beginning of March, the Russian National Institute of Automotive Engineering (NAMI), will deliver 16 vehicles to the Federal Security Service.
According to the report, the "caravan" project requires the use of a unified modular platform to build three kinds of cars - extended cars, three carriages and minibuses for the country's number one - 12.4 billion roubles. The budget allocation for the project is 12.4 billion rubles.
According to the report, the news came about five years ago about five years ago for the president's construction of the Soviet Union. According to the R&D unit's plan, the new car will be equipped with 800-horsepower engines and armor, and the entire vehicle will weigh 6 tons.
It is reported that the engineering and technical team of Porsche AG in Germany was involved in the development of power units.
According to the TASS news agency reported on January 16th, Manturov told reporters that the "caravan" series of cars will be retailed from 2019, and models of various configurations can be purchased.
“Starting next year,” the minister said, “from next year, there will be no restrictions on sales, whether bulletproof or luxurious.”
Russia's Ministry of Industry and Trade plans to increase the annual output of the "caravan" series of cars to more than 1,000 after 2020.
Manturov said: "We are now producing 18 vehicles at full capacity, this year's production is more than 70, next year to 200, the next year 300 or more."
