After the welcoming ceremony, Li Keqiang and Trudeau held the 2nd annual dialogue between Chinese and Canadian prime ministers.
Li Keqiang commented positively on the development of China-Canada relations over the past year
Li Keqiang said that the current economic globalization has continued to advance, and a new round of scientific and technological and industrial revolution has swept the world.
In order for China-Canada relations to maintain healthy and stable development, it is necessary to conform to the trend of the times.
Adhere to mutual respect, equal treatment, mutual benefit and win-win results, and constantly expand common interests.
Li Keqiang pointed out that practical cooperation between China and Canada is complementary and should expand two-way trade and investment, and enterprises of the two countries should be encouraged to invest in each other's countries.
Li Keqiang stressed that as an important country in the Asia-Pacific region and a major world trading country, it is in the common interests of the two sides to send a positive signal on the issue of promoting the liberalization and facilitation of trade and investment.
China's door to opening to the outside world will become more and more and better, and it will continue to be a hot spot for international investment.
Continuation of the friendship between the two countries
The Canadian side supports free trade and is willing to work with China to jointly promote globalization and free trade and contribute to global sustainable development.
The two sides also exchanged views on international and regional issues of common concern.
After the talks, the prime ministers of the two countries jointly witnessed the signing of bilateral cooperation documents in the fields of education, food safety and energy.
On the afternoon of the 4th, Li Keqiang and Canadian Prime Minister Trudeau jointly met with reporters.
Li Keqiang introduced the results of the 2nd China-Canada Prime Minister's annual dialogue.
He said that the two sides agreed to promote the process of globalization, maintain trade and investment liberalization and facilitation, and are willing to make joint efforts to explore the feasibility of the China-Canada Free Trade Agreement.
China is open to the negotiation process and content.
The two sides agreed to strengthen cooperation in tourism and aviation and intensify people-to-people and cultural exchanges between the two countries.
We will share opportunities, meet challenges together, and promote China-Canada relations at the golden stage.
Deepen cooperation in various fields, we are committed to common development and prosperity, and we are committed to building long-term, stable and active relations.
