Since the second half of 2009, Xiaoshan flower and wood sales have maintained a relatively high trend, especially in this spring, Xiaoshan seedling sales hit a record high again, sales increased sharply, prices rose sharply, according to statistics, from January to June this year Xiaoshan to achieve seedling sales revenue increased by 48% compared with the same period last year, the largest increase in nearly 20 years.
Shi Haiyong, deputy director of Xiaoshan District Forestry Bureau, said that with a good sales situation, Xiaoshan flower and wood production has also achieved rapid development.
In the past two years, the planting area of Xiaoshan flower trees has been expanded by 30,000 mu, and the total area has reached 180,000 mu; at the same time, it has actively developed outside the area, and Xiaoshan seedling farmers have established 80,000 mu of flower and wood bases all over the country, an increase of 30,000 mu compared with 2008.
At the same time as the planting area is expanding, the quality of seedlings has also been continuously improved, the value of the nursery has been continuously improved, large-scale and high-quality seedlings have been retained, and some seedlings have been sold.
Shi Haiyong also reminded that in the face of the current prosperity of production and sales, producers should calmly face, objective analysis, not only to see that the society's demand for flowers and trees will be long-term and increasing, but also to recognize that the market competition will be more intense.
On the morning of July 13, Beijing time, the U.S. Somaltus company filed a lawsuit with the East Texas District Court, accusing Apple of infringing a battery technology patent it applied for in 2010.
The company has previously sued ASUS, Lenovo, Samsung, Sony and Toshiba with the same patents.
According to the lawsuit, the iPhone 6s and similar Apple devices violated U.S. patent No. 7,657, 386, known as the Integrated Battery Services System.
Plaintiff hopes to obtain cash compensation or charge patent fees for infringing equipment after the judgment has been announced.
Judging from the indictment, the plaintiff appeared to believe that the iPhone’s fast-charging feature infringed the company’s patents.
