According to leaked phone records, Trump pressured Mexico to pay for a border wall.
The Washington Post divulged a transcript of a phone call between U.S. President Donald Trump and the leaders of Mexico and Australia.
On January 27, in a phone call with Mexican President Enrique Pena Nieto, Trump urged him to stop saying publicly that he would not pay for the proposed border wall.
The President of the United States reportedly expressed his displeasure at his public attacks on the wall, and Putron allegedly said to him: “Don’t tell the media.”
During the presidential campaign, Trump promised to build a wall on the southern border of the United States and solemnly announced that Mexico would be required to pay for the project.
A transcript of a phone call between him and Australian Prime Minister Malcolm Turnbull was also released, which showed tense exchanges between them.
Trump told Turnbull that it was “ridiculous”, “unsavory” and “stupid” that the U.S. had advised the U.S. to ban the resettlement of refugees while now sticking to a deal brokered by the Obama administration that would make him look like a “fool.”
Trump hung up after telling Turnbull that “this was the most unpleasant call today.”
