SEOUL, Jan. 9 (Xinhua) -- South Korea and North Korea concluded high-level talks in Panmunjom on the evening of January 9, and the two sides issued a joint statement to reach an agreement on the DPRK's participation in the Pyeongchang Winter Olympics and the military sector talks between the two sides.
According to the joint statement issued by the two sides, the DPRK will send a high-level delegation and a delegation of the National Olympic Committee to participate in the Pyeongchang Winter Olympics.
In addition, the DPRK will also send athletes troupes, cheerleaders, art troupes, press troupes and other groups to visit South Korea; the ROK side will provide the necessary facilities for this.
The two Koreas also reached an agreement to ease the current military tensions and decided to hold inter-Korean military sector talks.
The report analyzed the results of a questionnaire survey of 1,045 foreign tourists who visited Seoul in December.
According to the report, the per capita shopping volume of foreign tourists is 1.06 million won.
Among them, the per capita shopping volume of Chinese tourists is 2.13 million won, which is 6.5 times that of Japanese tourists and 3.2 times that of American and European tourists.
When asked about the purpose of visiting Seoul, 62.2% of Chinese tourists answered "shopping" and 94.9% of Chinese tourists bought cosmetics.
96.3% of Chinese tourists shop in urban duty-free shops and spend 1.56 million won per capita.
