McKee Garcia and Vasily Lomachenko met for the first time to discuss a possible decisive battle in the future.
Vásili Lomachenko and McKee Garcia, currently in a state of possible conflict, will be held shortly after their first meeting on Thursday.
They were in separate rooms in Los ESPN’s office in Los Angeles, where undefeated World’s Boxing Council Lightweight champion Garcia took the lead in walking down the hallway to greet Lomachenko, the world’s boxing organization champion.
At Saturday’s Showtime, the umpires unanimously confirmed that Garcia had defeated four-zone world champion Adrian Broner to victory, both of whom had become among the top five players in the same heavyweight list.
Garcia stretched out his right hand and said, “Champion, how are you?”
Good luck to you.”
At 7 a.m. on ESPN on Saturday night, Lomachenko defeated Miguel Mariaga to secure his position.
When the two of them were photographed, Lomachenko’s agent, Eggis Klimas, pointed out that the potential showdown between the two runners depended on “perfect size.”
“I used to be lightweight,” Garcia said.
“I raised the level to play Brouna (140 pounds), but I didn’t weigh as much.
Compared to 140 pounds, my weight is very low.
I’d like to go back to being lightweight.
And he has to be lightweight (135 pounds) before we can fight against each other.
That’s exactly what the fans want.
Then we'll satisfy them."
Lomachenko agrees.
“The boxing world needs this fight.”
Clemes asked him whether he should charge a per-charge, and part of his strategy was to get Lomachenko to make his debut match with a 135-pounder later this year in order to make a date next summer with Garcia (37-0, 30 knockout rounds). Garcia is also interested in a showdown with the winner of the Jorge Linares-Luke Campbell after the Lightweight Boxing Championship on September 23.
"Because all the fans are asking this question, the battle may be a pay-per-view fee," Garcia said. After that, he was open to playing online with the best financial options.
“We’re the main ones.
It is impossible for anyone else to get so much attention.
“As long as they’re ready...”
Garcia praised Lomachenko as “a fantastic runner” and is likely to watch his boxing match on Saturday.
But Lomachenko hesitated about Garcia's accolades, saying he thought the three-dipartment title from Riverside looked "slow. I'm sorry, McKee ... you'll be eliminated."
Garcia said the focus is to show the strength of the fist, and then boxing.
They all said that they could feel the momentum of their boxing match.
“It’s a battle that needs to be fought,
The level of attention and popularity is beyond the reach of other boxing matches.
“I’m very happy to participate,” Garcia said.
Lomachenko said: “I’ve been waiting for the top fighters, this time it’s McKee’s turn.
It's going to be a great fight."
