China's National Development and Reform Commission's official statement on the 11th Five-Year emission reduction target was completed ahead of schedule, so that the steel industry, which is limited by limited power production, has a strong expectation of resuming production.
Although the steel mill has not yet received a clear notice from the local government to announce the completion of energy conservation and emission reduction work, the industry estimates that around December 15, 2010, steel mills that were originally limited in various places will complete the resumption of production successively, and the steel price may begin to come under pressure.
There has not yet been notified of the end of the power limit, but in fact, the pressure of various enterprises has been much smaller than in September and October, a private steel enterprises in Hebei Province told reporters.
Some parts of Hebei have repeatedly issued power-restriction production documents, and once adopted the method of force-pull the gate to restrict the production of enterprises.
The reporter learned from the local enterprises that at present, steel mills in most parts of Hebei have returned to work, and the pressure to limit production has eased.
Zhang Tieshan, an analyst of my steel network, expects that due to the winter in the north, the terminal demand for construction steel will gradually change from strong to weak.
Coupled with the gradual termination of energy conservation and emission reduction, around December 15, most steel mills will basically resume production, and products will arrive in various markets before New Year's Day.
The increase in the supply of resources will put a certain amount of pressure on the price of steel, which is the right rise.
