On the 18th, the Economic and Commercial Affairs Department of the Italian Embassy in China held the China-Italy Environmental Protection Fair, and people from enterprises and scientific research institutions of the two countries exchanged extensive views and reached a positive consensus on the cooperation between the two countries in the field of renewable resources under the new situation.
It is reported that China's participants mainly include China Renewable Resources Development Co., Ltd. and China's international technology transfer and cooperation network, and the Italian side is composed of global energy and environment exchange organizations and other institutions.
The Italian representative said that Italy has a variety of environmental protection technologies and solutions in the field of renewable resources, and proposed to carry out pilot projects with China in industrial waste treatment, waste oil treatment and waste incineration treatment equipment, while looking forward to promoting the experience of environmental protection cooperation with China to the rest of the world.
The latest results of the age assessment test for asylum seekers in Sweden have been released.
Using the latest approach to medically assessing their age, more than 80 per cent of participants were judged to be older than 18, but not everyone was convinced of their accuracy.
Sweden’s National Center for French Medicine (R?ttsmedicinalverket) began testing earlier this year.
After being accused of failing to accurately assess the age of some of the refugees who claimed to be minors, the Swedish Migration Board (Migrationsverket) designed these tests with a view to conducting a more accurate age assessment during the asylum process.
So far, the Swedish Immigration Department has sent 6,880 test subjects, and the Forensic Science Center has now released the results of a total of 2,481 test subjects between mid-March 2017 and July 31, 2017.
Eighty per cent (2002 people) were determined to be 18 years of age or older, but in another 25 tests, the Swedish National Centre for Forensic Science determined that the subjects were “probably 18 years of age or older.”
In 432 tests, the result was “probably under the age of 18.”
The test is only available to people whose age is in doubt.
According to John Glenson of the Center for Forensic Medicine, these results are consistent with those in previous months.
He told The Local: “These figures are not very different from those of the previous months, the figures are very consistent.”
A higher proportion of cases that have been determined to be 18 years of age or older does not necessarily mean that these asylum-seekers lied about their age.
In May, the center released 581 test results and said 442 cases “indicated that the subject was 18 years of age or older.”
Newspaper Svenska Dagbladet looked at 581 published test results and found that 243 of them had publicly stated that they would be 18 years of age this year.
An X-ray examination of the wisdom teeth, an MRI scan of the joints, and the results were then analyzed by dentists and radiologists, and this medical evaluation method is also questioned in some areas.
One of the skeptics was Claude Marcus, an endocrinologist at Karolin College, whose work included assessing a person’s biological maturity to determine if they experienced puberty earlier or later than normal.
“I have a reason to think this way, and I don’t think the way the measurements used should be like that.
Determining the biological age in this way is very inaccurate.
“If we can’t guarantee the accuracy, we shouldn’t pretend that we can.”
Gülenson of the Forensic Science Center, however, defends the accuracy of these tests: “It’s generally said that there’s a very small risk of not determining whether a child is an adult.”
The biggest risk is that the person is just under the age of 18, which accounts for about 10 per cent.
The governor of West Virginia announced a change of party.
On Thursday night, West Virginia Democratic Governor Jim Justice announced at President Trump’s rally that he would change partisanship.
“If you don’t like it or don’t like it, the Democrats are gone from me,” the gubernator’s judge said.
“Today, after a lot of prayers and a great deal of thought, I’m going to tell you... Today I’m going to tell you as a West Virginian that I can’t help you anymore as a Democratic governor.”
Cheers broke out at the rally.
“Tomorrow, I’m going to change my party to the Republican Party,” Jastis added.
“As a coach, I’m going to say that it’s time to start another game.”
At an earlier rally in West Virginia, Trump promised a major announcement.
Mr. Trump won 42 per cent of the vote in West Virginia, and Jastis didn’t support Democratic candidate Hillary Clinton.
According to Forbes, Jastis was selected as the state’s only billionaire in 2016.
“Forbes” pointed out that he inherited his father's coal industry and owns coal mines in all five states.
At present, he is worth about 1.59 billion US dollars.
At the same time, the Republican National Committee said in a statement on Thursday night: "Governor Jastis' party is another blow to the Democratic Party, which not only does not prevent our country from becoming great again, it will make our country great again."
“The Democratic Party currently has only 15 governors and has the lowest number of state legislatures in control of the all-time, and Governor Justice’s statement is the latest rejection of a party that has lost leadership from top to bottom and can’t find a positive unified slogan,” Republican National Committee chairwoman Rona McDaniel said in a statement to CBS News.
