Renmin's mid-range price of 6.4401 depreciated 66 basis points
Macroeconomic Tencent Finance 2018-01-18 09:50
On January 18, the middle price of the RMB against the U.S. dollar fell by 66 basis points in the previous trading day, ending the previous five consecutive increases.
In the overnight market, the U.S. dollar picks up, and the U.S. dollar's index goes out in the form of the V word, as of 07:30 Beijing time.
According to the Federal Reserve’s economic beige book, almost all of its 12 Fed regions reported modest to moderate growth in economic activity at the start of 2018 and remained optimistic about the outlook for this year.
At the same time, the U.S. unemployment rate remained at 4.1% in December, the lowest since 2000, and companies are expected to raise wages in the next few months.
Federal Fed officials generally believe that the tax reform is a factor supporting this moderately stronger economic outlook, and the Fed is forecasting economic growth of 2.5% in 2018 and raising interest rates three times.
Market participants pointed out that in recent times, the European Central Bank's monetary policy tightening is expected to push up the exchange rate of the euro, the U.S. dollar index continues to decline, and the exchange rate of the RMB against the U.S. dollar is corresponding to a wave of rapid rise, but at present, the European Central Bank is unlikely to adjust its policy stance very quickly.
It is worth noting that as the market's expectations for the yuan become more stable, the attractiveness of RMB assets to foreign investors has gradually become prominent.
The People's Bank of China authorized the China Foreign Exchange Trading Center to announce that on January 18, 2018, the RMB exchange rate in the inter-bank foreign exchange market was: 1 US dollar to 6.4401 yuan, 1 euro to RMB 7.8482 yuan, 100 yen to RMB 5.7854 yuan, 1 Hong Kong to RMB 0.82399 yuan, 1 pound to RMB 8.9017 yuan, 1 Australian dollar to RMB 5.1302, 1 New Zealand dollar to RMB 4.7779, 1 NZ dollar to foreign currency, 1 NZ dollar to ��an to �� , 1 Swiss dollar to RMB .
At 7:50 a.m. today (March 10), there was an explosion at a chemical plant in Xinxiang County, Henan Province, and black smoke was raised at the scene.
The reporter of the Beijing News learned from the Propaganda Department of Xinxiang County Party Committee that a total of one person was injured in the explosion.
The video released by local netizens showed smoke billowing at the scene of the explosion, accompanied by noise.
Some netizens said that this morning, the explosion site was a chemical plant located in Xiaoji Town, Xinxiang County, Henan Province.
The reporter of the Beijing News learned that the incident chemical factory is Henan Xinxiang Liutong Industrial Co., Ltd.
According to public information, the above-mentioned enterprises were established in February 2002 and include the manufacturing of chemical products in their business scope.
This afternoon, the Propaganda Department of the Xinxiang County Party Committee responded that the explosion took place at 7:50 a.m. At present, the fire has been effectively controlled, and one person has suffered minor injuries.
The reporter of the Beijing News noticed that as early as 2015, the chemical factory involved was exposed by the media, including Henan TV, due to illegal sewage discharge.
