President Xi Jinping met with Russian Prime Minister Dmitry Medvedev at the Diaoyutai State Guesthouse on November 1.
Xi Jinping welcomed Medvedev's visit to China immediately after the conclusion of China's 19th National Congress, emphasizing that Russia is China's largest neighbor.
Comprehensive and strategic collaboration partners
China's clear goal and firm determination to develop and deepen China-Russia relations will not change.
The Chinese side is willing to work with the Russian side to expand cooperation in various fields and all-round, and strengthen coordination and coordination and cooperation in international affairs.
Advancing the building of a community with a shared future for mankind
It is believed that the China-Russia comprehensive strategic partnership of coordination will seize new opportunities at a new starting point, show a new climate, and achieve new results.
Xi Jinping pointed out that China and Russia should give full play to the overall and coordinated role of the prime minister's regular meeting mechanism, and strengthen cooperation in energy, equipment manufacturing, agriculture.
Cooperation in aerospace and other fields will continue to enhance the content of scientific and technological innovation in the cooperation between the two sides, and the digital economy fields such as big data, the Internet of Things, and smart cities will continue to
As a new growth point of cooperation
It is necessary to do a good job in docking with the Eurasian Economic Union, strive to promote projects such as coastal international transport corridors, and jointly carry out cooperation in the development and utilization of Arctic shipping lanes.
Creating an Ice Silk Road
Promote local exchanges and cooperation between the two countries and further consolidate the public opinion foundation of bilateral relations.
Medvedev conveyed Russian President Vladimir Putin's cordial greetings and good wishes to President Xi Jinping and concluded the victory of the 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of China.
Xi Jinping was re-elected General Secretary of the Communist Party of the Communist Party of China to express warm congratulations.
We have made more positive progress in cooperation in the fields of economy, energy, investment, innovation, humanities, the Eurasian Economic Union and the Belt and Road.
The Russian side is very satisfied with this, and is willing to further strengthen exchanges and cooperation with China in various fields and strengthen communication and coordination in international and regional affairs.
Ding Xuexiang and Yang Jiechi participated in the meeting.
Subsequently, the prime ministers of the two countries looked at the disaggregation ceremony.
After the welcoming ceremony, the prime ministers of the two countries co-chaired the twenty-second regular meeting of Chinese and Russian prime ministers.
Li Keqiang said that under the impetus of President Xi Jinping and President Putin, China-Russia relations continue to bear new fruits.
The 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of the Communist Party of China has just been successfully concluded.
The election produced a new Central Committee of the Communist Party of China with Comrade Xi Jinping as the core, which established Xi Jinping's socialist thought with Chinese characteristics in the new era.
The guiding ideology that our party must adhere to for a long period of time has clarified China's future development goals.
As the largest developing country, China's development is the foundation and the key to solving all problems.
China and Russia see each other's development as an important opportunity.
The two countries face broader prospects for docking development strategies and deepening all-round cooperation, which will also contribute more and more positive forces to peace and development between the two countries, the region and even the world.
Li Keqiang and Medvedev listened to the relevant mechanisms of the two countries, the working reports of Chinese Presidents Zhang Gaoli, Wang Yang and Liu Yandong, as well as the Russian president.
Create a better tomorrow for relations between the two countries.
Medvedev congratulates the Communist Party of China on the successful convening of the 19th National Congress of the Communist Party of China, saying that the Russian side is willing to deepen cooperation with China in traditional fields such as energy, infrastructure construction, production capacity and aerospace.
Open up cooperation in emerging fields such as e-commerce and small and medium-sized enterprises, strengthen people-to-people and cultural exchanges, and promote the continuous development of the Russia-China comprehensive strategic partnership of coordination.
After the meeting, Li Keqiang and Medvedev signed a joint communique on the 22nd regular meeting of Chinese and Russian prime ministers, and jointly witnessed investment.
The signing of nearly 20 bilateral cooperation documents in the fields of energy, local cooperation, humanities, agriculture, customs, quality inspection, aerospace and finance.
After the signing ceremony, the prime ministers of the two countries met with reporters and answered questions.
Li Keqiang introduced the outcome of the meeting and stressed China's willingness to continue mutual respect, equality and mutual benefit.
On the basis of common development, we should promote China-Russia relations and cooperation in various fields, and promote the establishment of a new type of international relations with win-win cooperation as the core.
We also need to create more cooperative growth points.
We must not only focus on giving full play to the advantages of large and powerful large enterprises in the two countries, and strengthen cooperation in strategic large-scale projects in the fields of energy, aerospace, aviation and cross-border infrastructure, but also make good use of the advantages of small and medium-sized enterprises.
Support them to open up new areas of cooperation and accelerate innovation for the practical cooperation between the two countries.
In the afternoon of the same day, Li Keqiang and Medvedev jointly attended the closing ceremony of the Sino-Russian media exchange year and delivered a speech.
The positive results and social repercussions of the year of media exchanges are highly appraised.
Li Keqiang said in his speech that two years ago, the heads of state of the two countries jointly decided and announced the launch of the Sino-Russian media exchange year.
It shows that China and Russia, as comprehensive strategic cooperation partners, have a high degree of mutual trust in politics, have a cultural connection, and have an objective and friendly attitude towards each other.
To build an important bridge and link, Li Keqiang pointed out that China and Russia are countries with long-standing cultural traditions and deep cultural heritage.
The media of the two countries also have their own characteristics.
Through the year of media exchanges, the two sides have improved their understanding, deepened their friendship, and promoted mutual learning among the media.
It has become a special event in the history of international media exchanges.
Today's closing ceremony is not the end, it is a new starting point, I believe it will open a new chapter of Sino-Russian media cooperation and raise a new sail of people-to-people and cultural exchanges.
To promote China-Russia relations to embark on a new journey of generation-to-generation friendship
The relations between the two countries have given new connotations, brought about new opportunities, and fully reflected the level of friendship between the two peoples and the strategic significance of bilateral relations.
