Beijing "university dredging" new measures: tens of thousands of teachers and students will be stationed in Changping new campus
The opening ceremony of the new campus of Beijing University of Chemical Technology was held in Changping District of Beijing on the 2nd, and the green campus covering an area of 1,800 acres was officially put into use.
The reporter learned from the ceremony that in order to strengthen the capital's core function and manage the "big city disease", in recent years, under the background of the coordinated development of the Beijing-Tianjin-Hebei and non-capital functions, Beijing has accelerated the relief of universities in the central urban area to the suburbs, and the teachers and students of some colleges and universities are successively moving to new campuses in Shunyi, Daxing, Fangshan and other suburbs.
North chemical new campus is located in Changping Nankou town, covers an area of 1,800 acres, 40 kilometers from the urban area, is one of the key projects in Beijing to relieve non-capital functions.
At present, the second phase of construction is expected to be fully launched by the end of this year, and it is planned to meet the needs of nearly 20,000 undergraduates, graduate students and teaching staff after completion.
