The president of the Croatian Football Association, Davao-Suk, said in an interview that participating in the Chinese Cup is very meaningful for Croatian football, and the bonus figures for the Chinese Cup are very large.
You don't have to buy more than 8000 kinds of products without tariffs.
At the regular press conference held by the Ministry of Commerce on January 11, the spokesman of the Ministry of Commerce said that as of now, there are 15 free trade agreements that have been implemented in China, involving 23 countries and regions, covering more than 8,000 kinds of zero-tariff imported products.
At the same time, imported cosmetics, Icelandic salmon, Chilean red wine, ASEAN tropical fruits... you don’t have to spend a lot of money to buy these products anymore.
At present, China has signed 16 free trade agreements with 24 countries and regions, and has implemented 15, covering more than 8,000 zero-tariff import products.
Taking agricultural products as an example, with the implementation of the free trade agreement, consumers can taste agricultural products from different production areas with high-quality and low-cost products throughout the year.
For example, in tropical fruits such as durians, lychees and dragon fruit in ASEAN, import tariffs have been reduced from 15% to 30% to zero tariffs.
The import tariff on Icelandic salmon has been reduced from 10% to 12% to zero.
For Georgian and Chilean wines, the import tariff has been reduced from 14% to 30% to zero tariffs.
New Zealand's special agricultural products such as beef and milk powder have significantly reduced taxes.
In the case of industrial products, for example, the import tariff on some cosmetics in Switzerland has been reduced to zero;
The import tariff on some watches has been reduced by 50%, and it will be reduced to zero tariffs after a few years.
South Korea's refrigerators, rice cookers, massagers, beauty meters and other products have been reduced import tariffs by 40%, and will be reduced to zero tariffs in a few years;
There have also been large-scale tax cuts in consumer electronics.
At the same time, the zero-tariff products under the free trade zone also include the intermediate products and raw materials needed for the manufacture of many domestic terminal consumer goods, which has also promoted the structural upgrading of domestic consumer goods to a certain extent.
Ministry of Commerce Spokesperson Gao Feng said that China's total imports of nearly one-third of the products can enjoy preferential tariff treatment in the free trade agreement, most of which are terminal consumer goods, which has brought tangible benefits to consumers.
Further reduction of import tariffs on consumer goods
Since December 1, 2017, China's import tariffs on some consumer goods have been adjusted to further reduce import tariffs on consumer goods, covering various types of consumer goods such as food, health care products, pharmaceuticals, daily necessities, clothing, shoes and hats, household equipment, culture and entertainment, and department stores, involving a total of 187 8-bit tax numbers.
The average tax rate for this group of consumer goods will be reduced from 17.3% to 7.7%, which will be almost cut!
Since January 1, 2018, China has also made partial adjustments to other import and export tariffs.
The import tariff on lip balm, eye shadow, perfume and other cosmetics is reduced from 10% to 5%.
After the reduction of tariffs, it means that consumers do not have to shop on their behalf, and they don't have to travel abroad to buy favorite foreign products.
2018 Yiwu imported goods shopping festival: imports of red wine, snacks, fruits ... are all cheap!
Foreign report: at the end of the year, U.S. mall regulations vary greatly, shopping returns need to be cautious
The new network on December 29th.
According to the U.S. "World Daily" reported that just after Christmas, it ushered in a wave of returns.
According to the American Broadcasting Corporation (ABC), more than half of the goods sold last Christmas have been returned.
In addition, there are readers who have repeatedly exposed online shopping to be cheated, and consumers need to pay more attention when shopping on informal websites.
Generally speaking, large-scale shopping companies have regular and reasonable return procedures, but if they buy gifts or e-commerce purchases from some small stores, they must be careful.
On December 1, local time, in an online store that specializes in selling printed jackets, Ms. Rowangang spent more than 60 yuan (US dollars, the same below) to buy a coat, and the results have not yet been sent.
She sent an e-mail to the customer and did not reply.
Some netizens broke the news that they traveled to the United States last year to buy a mobile phone from third-party sellers, and after sending it, it was found that there was a box of plaster.
After knowing that it has been cheated, apply for a refund from the website, and it is good to get a full refund.
However, some customers also believe that the website refund service is not 100% perfect.
Mr. Wang, a Chinese resident in Northern California, said that he had purchased an expedited delivery service of a certain website twice, and an expedited service of four yuan at a time, but it was not delivered on time twice.
After applying for a refund, there was no response.
Large shopping malls or shopping malls have a better return policy.
Most Macy’s products will be fully refunded within 180 days.
However, the goods must remain "originally", and they must have purchase vouchers, such as receipts or bank purchase records.
If there is no certificate, customers can also obtain mall points, which can be used to purchase other goods.
Target usually has a 90-day return period for general goods, and electronic products are usually 15 days.
However, the return period of electronic and entertainment goods purchased between November 1 and December 25, 2017 has been extended to 30 days.
It should be noted that the 30-day refund period begins on December 25, that is, it must be returned before January 25, 2018.
The ultimate shopping experience, the new era of business district shopping development
More than a decade ago, our country in general is still in the seller's market, and people's choices are limited and their needs are limited.
However, after ten years of development, the market has already realized the transformation from the seller's market to the buyer's market, and today's consumer tastes have become more difficult, and they are no longer satisfied with a simple "one-handed delivery" shopping behavior.
Therefore, how to let consumers get an extreme shopping experience has become the next competitive point for real estate developers.
Among the many factors that affect the shopping experience of consumers, the impact of shopping centers in the business circle is the most significant.
Let's see how urban builders focus on the shopping experience.
There are no two exactly the same leaves in the world, and there are no two completely identical shopping malls, and a well-known shopping center must have its own characteristics.
For example, Turkey's world-famous Kanyon shopping center, its unique wavy architectural design is inspired by the Grand Canyon (Canyon), so it is called the homophonic Kanyon, walking in Kanyon's 200-meter-long walkway.
In addition to canyon-style design, in the middle of the shopping center, there is also a large-scale oval-shaped performance venue with a unique appearance, often holding special performances.
Because of the design of the open platform, tourists can walk on each floor to look at the activities carried out in the "canyon", and have the effect of shifting scenery.
At home, known as China's first forest-style walking consumer market, the Nanjing Forest Moore commercial street combines shopping with ecology and fairy tales.
7000 square meters of green square, 3,000 square meters of rooftop water platform, the project is composed of 9 individual buildings, between the buildings in the air corridor, the overall sinking of the courtyard design, taking the geographical edge of the French sycamore tree for the skin of the building, the roof of the water platform, to create a forest-like feeling.
Walking into the forest mole is like accidentally falling into the rabbit hole in Alice's roaming adventure, climbing along the tree trunk will surround the building, meadows and clear springs, bringing people into a forest full of vitality and vitality.
Also in Chongqing, Longhu to build the Lijia waterfront business district, the planning of hundreds of businesses, plans to introduce more than 50 international top exclusive flagship stores in the future, more than 100 international top brands and more than 500 well-known brands at home and abroad, to become a service industry agglomeration, distinctive theme of the commercial center.
Not only that, the waterfront business district will also be ecologically integrated into the building, TOD public transportation-oriented, a collection of fashion shopping, life services, catering, entertainment, education, sports in one, in order to bring consumers the ultimate shopping experience while also leading them to enjoy Chongqing's unique "waterfront culture", the perfect integration of shopping and water entertainment and leisure.
It can be found that at present, a part of the real estate enterprises have insight into the discovery trajectory of this new urban business, and industry insiders said that this consumer experience as the center, how to combine shopping and experience consumption mode will also be the mainstream of future urban development.
Today's business circle is not only a distribution of goods, but also a comprehensive place for the integration of art and culture and creative themes, and also carries people's responsibilities for living in the city.
Therefore, at the same time to meet the one-stop material needs of consumers to eat and drink Tesco, to maximize the transmission of cultural and artistic multi-level spiritual needs, livable residential demand, is bound to be the commanding heights of the future development of the business circle.
In Chongqing, Guoxing's northern shore is located in Jiangbei, close to Guanyin Bridge, the world's commercial essence, the international giants are surrounded, and first-class brands come together to connect closely with international fashion.
It’s busy here and it’s the essence of the world.
Dongyuan Jinyue has a better shopping environment, Dongyuan Jinyue is close to the Nan Ping business district, exclusive to the western and even the country's leading four-level three-dimensional transportation system, to enhance shopping comfort.
In addition, the landscaping and landscaping and landscape pavements of the two pedestrian streets of Huigong Road and Wanda Square have been upgraded, about 300 trees have been planted, and 40,000 square meters have been transformed, which has enhanced the image of the Nan Ping business district;
And Longhu Yuhu One, close to Chongqing's first low-density waterfront business district, is surrounded by nine parks, with a low density and a high degree of openness, which makes people more willing to stop, stop, and slowly enjoy the fun of shopping when shopping, rather than being surrounded by the flow of people in the back.
Today's commercial competition will only become more and more fierce, how to create a bloody road in the homogenization of the serious market and win the reputation of "shopping mecca" in the hearts of consumers in the future is worthy of serious consideration by all real estate developers.
It is not enough to rely on the differentiation strategy alone, and only those developers who really put consumers in their hearts, are in a hurry for consumers to think, and provide consumers with the ultimate and simple shopping experience can laugh in the storm-coming market.
Of course, in the end, I want to be most happy for the people of Chongqing, with such such a good shopping experience and business district, no one can imagine today's prosperity 10 years ago.
The festival: consumerism carnival conceals the price of the real environment
168.2 billion yuan, this is on November 11, 2017, "Tmall double eleven global carnival" within 24 hours, Tmall user consumption turnover.
Specifically, after the start of "double 11", Tmall's turnover exceeded 10 billion yuan in just 3 minutes, more than 20 billion yuan in 6 minutes and 05 seconds, and exceeded 100 billion yuan in 9 hours.
On this day, the total number of payments made by global consumers through Alipay reached 1.48 billion, an increase of 41% over last year.
These consumptions will result in 812 million logistics orders.
Whether it is Tmall online shopping platform or Alipay payment platform, they all belong to Ma Yun's Ali Group.
Ten years ago, no one would have thought that on November 11, the "singles day" subculture created by single young people for self-deprecation will be compiled by e-commerce and has become the "double 11" shopping carnival of today's phenomenon.
On November 11, 2009, for the first time, Alibaba used the marketing stagger of "singles day promotion": no one fell in love with you, so the "single dog" came to buy it online.
The result is surprising, on this day Taobao mall ("Tmall" predecessor) transaction volume exceeded 52 million yuan, which was 10 times the daily transaction volume at that time.
Since then, "double 11" has become Alibaba to create a shopping carnival, from the beginning of the domestic buyers and sellers of their own entertainment, and now the influx of global merchants, nine years have passed, Tmall "double 11" hundreds of billions of transactions has been more than 3,200 times that year, so that "Black Friday" can't wait.
Following Tmall's "double eleven" promotion, there are a number of e-commerce companies, of which "Jingdong" is the strongest.
"Jingdong" has its own shopping festival "6.18", but there is no "double 11" has a big impact, this year from November 1st to 11th, "Jingdong" cumulative sales reached 127.1 billion yuan.
After the "double 11", it was followed by a similar "double 12" discount carnival and Christmas New Year shopping schedule.
Crossing the New Year, waiting for Chinese consumers also before the Chinese New Year's purchase period, Valentine's Day shopping schedule, consumption, will not take a holiday.
The environmental problems brought about by instantaneous mass consumption have aroused the attention of professionals and institutions.
According to Xinhua Daily Telegraph, according to the usual standard of 0.2 kilograms per box in the industry, at least 300,000 tons of garbage were generated during this year's "double 11" period.
Liu Hua, director of the pollution prevention and control project of the Greenpeace East Asia Division, told the Sino-foreign dialogue that this year's "double 11" Tmall's order volume will produce 160,000 tons of packaging waste.
In 2016, the State Postal Administration issued a report, pointing out that during the "double 11" period in 2015 (November 11 to 16), the number of express shipments was about 780 million, using more than 3 billion woven bags, 9.922 billion boxes, 16.985 billion meters of tape, and the tape length can circle the Earth's Equator 425 times.
And this year, the National Postal Administration is expected to "double 11" express business volume is expected to exceed 1.5 billion pieces.
Wang Shi, manager of a waste incineration center in Beijing, told Xinhua that more than 2,000 tons of garbage entered every day after "double 11", which also exceeded the processing capacity of the incineration station.
The courier company has realized that the environmental pollution caused by the express delivery industry can not be considered.
Some e-commerce logistics companies, including Suning, have launched recyclable and reusable plastic courier boxes in front of "double 11", recycled bags that can be reused as shopping bags and garbage bags, etc., but the acceptance of troublesome consumers is not very high.
Ma Yun also called on the logistics industry to support "green packaging" and "green logistics" in Weibo.
This micro-blog has gained more than 68,000 "likes".
What kind of mobile payments do the Germans want?
Zhang Dongfang: The mobile payment war launched in Germany is not expected.
WeChat payment and Alipay only moved the battlefield to Europe, the competitors did not change, the seizure of the position did not change - the Chinese, this is called globalization?
Where there is an Alipay, there must be a WeChat payment.
In accordance with the agreement of the German electronic payment service provider Wirecard, WeChat Pay officially began to land in Germany in November this year, and has gradually deployed merchants in Europe.
The foreign reunion of the two "fellows" took place in Europe.
All along, Alipay and WeChat Pay on the path of globalization.
For China's global approach to mobile payment in China's mobile payment industry, Eric Consulting's "China's third-party mobile payment industry research report 2017" is summarized into two types: one is through strategic investment, experience output, equity and support for foreign local mobile payment enterprises.
The second is to promote mobile payment services to foreign merchants through the consumption behavior of Chinese tourists abroad, thereby changing the awareness and acceptance of China's mobile payment.
Indeed, the Chinese will win.
China's rapid economic development, coupled with a large population base, the spending of Chinese tourists in Europe is an attractive figure.
But it is also doomed, the Chinese mobile payment war launched in Germany is not expected.
WeChat payment and Alipay are just moving the battlefield to Europe, the competitors have not changed, the looting position has not changed - or the Chinese, this is also a globalization?
The more pioneering discussion is whether China's mobile payment can open up territory in Europe?
Take Germany for example.
The "new retail" by magic.
Chen Yilei and Yang Kaihan: When Amazon entered the world's top ten retailers, it announced its entry into bookstores and groceries, regardless of the timing and motivation.
In November 2015, Amazon opened its first brick-and-mortar bookstore in Seattle, followed by two bookstores in Portland and San Diego.
At the beginning of 2017, Amazon opened stores in New York, and plans to have at least eight stores by the end of the year.
Almost at the same time, Amazon announced the trial operation of its unmanned supermarket (Amazon Go), customers do not need to queu, do not need to checkout, enter the code, take the desired goods to leave, the purchase amount will be automatically deducted from the customer's Amazon account.
As far as Amazon is concerned, in the past few years, it is a very unexpected thing to act frequently in physical stores.
As early as the "open letter to shareholders" as early as 2007, CEO Jeff Bezos stressed that Amazon will not easily open physical stores, unless the following four conditions are met at the same time:
We must be confident that this new opportunity will pay off for the investment of our shareholders.
We must be convinced that this new opportunity is of great significance to the entire company;
We must be convinced that this new opportunity is ignored by the market.
We must be convinced that in this market, we have enough resources to make customer-oriented differentiation.
Bookshops and groceries are the most faltering classifications of the two brick-and-mortar retailers, as well as the first to fall after Amazon’s rise.
Amazon's entry into the world's top 10 retailers announced its entry into these two physical markets, regardless of the timing and motivation is very interesting.
Does Amazon’s practices run counter to the guarantees in a shareholder’s letter?
On the morning of October 13, 2016, at the 2016 Hangzhou · Yunqi conference, Alibaba Chairman of the Board of Directors Jack Ma delivered a keynote speech.
He said: "From next year, Alibaba will no longer mention the term 'e-commerce'.
The era of pure e-commerce will soon come to an end, the next ten or twenty years there will be no e-commerce, replaced by "new retail".
The combination of online, offline and logistics will lead to new retail.”
For a long time, the three words of "new retail" have been enchanted, and they are frequently used by people in the industry.
But what does “new retail” really mean?
If it is just a combination of online and offline, then the concept is not novel.
In 2016, eMarketer tracked the 180 largest e-commerce companies and estimated total e-commerce sales of about $200 billion, of which the largest 25 accounted for more than $159 billion.
Of these 25, 18 are traditional retailers that have only started operating online in the past five years (such as Macy’s, Nordstrom, Target, Gap, etc.).
Alibaba Group's 28.3 billion yuan investment in the Suning cloud business is also vivid.
On a global scale, retailers and e-commerce are shifting from a single channel to an omni-channel retail system covering physical stores, e-commerce, mobile and social media.
Does Ma Yun mention "new retail", which is more of a summary rather than an outlook for the future?
If not, what’s the difference between the omni-channel concept and “new retail”?
Perhaps, the key to the problem is not whether online and offline integration, but how to integrate.
Looking back at the past 20 years in the retail industry, the rise of e-commerce, like the rise of discount retailers in the early years, has focused on price and convenience.
Relying on these two pain points, e-commerce moved products with a very high degree of standardization, such as books and CDs, from offline to online.
With the development of online consumption habits and the continuous improvement of the customer experience, e-commerce has extended its tentacles to other categories and began to improve efficiency.
"Using the ideas and technologies of the Internet to comprehensively reform and upgrade the existing total of about 30 trillion social retailers has enabled the increasingly upgraded consumer demand of Chinese consumers to be effectively satisfied, making the entire process of commodity production, circulation, and service become more efficient due to the widespread use of the Internet and big data."
Therefore, the road of e-commerce is a path of surface-to-asset-to-asset and actual heavy assets.
"Light" refers to fixed assets, staffing, management processes and other burdens are not as large as the traditional retail industry; "heavy" refers to the need for huge investment in logistics, warehousing and other aspects.
The change of logistics methods ensures the high efficiency of e-commerce.
According to the news of the Chinese government network, Premier Li Keqiang presided over the executive meeting of the State Council on April 28, which believed that expanding domestic consumer demand was an important measure for steady growth and structural adjustment.
The meeting determined that the relevant departments should urgently come up with specific plans on the basis of scientific assessment.
For some foreign consumer goods with high domestic consumer demand, by the end of June this this year to reduce import tariffs, and gradually expand the scope of tax reduction goods;
In combination with the reform of the tax system, we will improve the consumption tax policy of mass consumer goods such as clothing and cosmetics, and comprehensively adjust the tax scope, tax rate and collection link;
Increase and restore duty-free stores at ports of entry, rationally expand duty-free varieties, increase a certain amount of duty-free purchases, and facilitate domestic consumers to purchase foreign products in the country;
We will further promote the facilitation of shopping customs clearance and tax rebates for overseas tourists, and strictly implement the requirements for active tax declaration of entry items in accordance with the law.
Develop inspection and quarantine policies to support cross-border e-commerce imports, and clean up unreasonable fees for imports;
Accelerating China's product brand promotion projects, supporting the development of physical stores, and achieving online and offline interaction.
Regulate the order of the market, strictly crack down on counterfeiting and shoddy, and promote the survival of the fittest.
So that consumers can be comfortable and easy to shop.
