On January 18, Alibaba held an e-commerce poverty alleviation summit dialogue meeting in Chongqing and announced that it will promote accurate poverty alleviation and rural revitalization by exploring a new model of "Internet + poverty alleviation".
This is after putting forward a rural strategy, launching a rural Taobao project, launching an agricultural poverty alleviation platform, and the establishment of the Alibaba Poverty Alleviation Fund, Ali has once again "increased" the fight against poverty.
Poverty alleviation is one of China's most important national strategies.
All-out poverty has never been eradicated in China for thousands of years.
E-commerce poverty alleviation is an innovative measure for a new round of poverty alleviation and development, and it is an important starting point to achieve accurate poverty alleviation and accurate poverty alleviation.
The central government attaches great importance to and pointed out that it can give full play to the role of the Internet in promoting poverty alleviation, promote precision poverty alleviation and precision poverty alleviation, and allow agricultural products to come out of the countryside through the Internet."
Therefore, as early as 2014, Ali put forward the rural strategy, with big data cloud computing and globalization as the three core strategies of Ali in the next 20 years.
In the same year, Ali launched the rural Taobao (village Tao) project to recruit "village number two" in the countryside and lead farmers to get rid of poverty through e-commerce.
In 2017, Ali cooperated with the business department to build a rural poverty alleviation channel, which is currently docked with 13 provinces and 120 poverty-stricken counties at the national level.
There have been 2,118 Taobao villages spawned by the Ali platform.
Among them, nearly 400 appeared in provincial poverty-stricken counties, and 33 appeared in poverty-stricken counties in 13 countries.
In 2017, on Alibaba's Chinese retail platform, Taobao Village's sales nationwide reached 120 billion yuan.
Zhang Yong said that in the face of the national strategy of poverty alleviation, Ali has been thinking about how to make good use of the innovation capabilities of Ali economy such as science and technology, big data, and cloud computing to find a new way out of poverty.
Among them, Muratao is the main carrier platform for Ali's e-commerce to get rid of poverty, and through a new link to the Internet for direct sales.
In the planting process, the village and Ant Financial jointly carried out agricultural tools and small loan support.
In 2017, among 832 state-level poverty-stricken prefectures, Ant Financial served 795, providing them with convenient payment, credit and other services.
Cainiao to deal with warehousing and logistics, Tmall is responsible for sales, Aliyun's big data to guide agricultural production and further improve the supply standards, quality and market competitiveness of agricultural products.
The development of e-commerce out of poverty requires not only products, sales channels and industrial planning, but also talents.
Through the e-commerce courses held by Taobao University, Ali teaches farmers standardized, quality and large-scale planting methods, and realizes the combination of "poverty alleviation + mental support", so that farmers can sustainably get rid of poverty.
These courses already cover about 92 per cent of the country ' s poverty-stricken counties.
The idea of poverty alleviation of "public welfare mentality and commercial means" can also ensure that Ali can achieve "true poverty alleviation" in poverty alleviation.
Ma Yun, chairman of Alibaba's board of directors, has said that poverty alleviation should be divided into three stages: poverty alleviation, poverty alleviation and wealth.
Poverty alleviation is teaching people to fish, getting out of poverty is teaching people to fish, getting rich is to make a "fish pond" for farmers, so that farmers can raise fish.
The industrial poverty alleviation driven by e-commerce is to make fish ponds.
In terms of industrial poverty alleviation, the Luochuan apple industry poverty alleviation model created by Ali in cooperation with Shaanxi Luochuan has been copied and promoted by relevant departments as examples throughout the country.
Ali e-commerce poverty alleviation work has also been recognized by the decision-making level.
The e-commerce enterprises represented by Alibaba have been sent messages to ensure that farmers increase production and income through online and offline channels.
A number of village and Ant Financial employees have also been invited to the United Nations and Africa to share e-commerce's experience in poverty alleviation.
At present, the China office of the United Nations World Food Programme has been working with the village to carry out e-commerce industry poverty alleviation in Anhui and other places.
The "Third New Economic Think Tank Conference" co-organized by the Ali Research Institute and the China Foresight think tank was held on January 16, and Zhang Li, director of the e-commerce institute of the Research Institute of the Ministry of Commerce, attended and made a speech.
In fact, she believes that our globalization ignores the most important issues, that is, the body and use of globalization, as well as the problem of the stage of globalization.
In this way, a lot of people think that globalization is stagnant, and many developed and developing countries have a different attitude towards globalization in the new stage.
The second concept is the problem of the mid-term stage of globalization, and what are the constraints of the medium-term stage of globalization?
Constraints on the foundations of the economic environment are constrained precisely by the changes in the economic foundation of globalization.
At the end of 2017, the global economic adjustment has basically ended, and it will enter a new round of growth after 2018, and the next round of growth must be driven by raw products.
