U.S. Changes to Green Card Regulations
The media quoted President Donald Trump as saying that the United States will launch a new immigration plan and modify the green card regulations.
The plan aims to reduce the number of legal immigrants to 50,000 people per year, and temporary work visas, as well as family-oriented visa applications, will be subject to stricter restrictions.
The new rules were proposed by the Republican Party and supported by the president.
The draft law will be discussed in both chambers.
U.S. media quoted Trump as saying: "This law will reduce poverty, raise wages, save hundreds of billions of dollars for taxpayers, and achieve these benefits by changing the way the United States issues green cards to citizens of other countries."
The law would replace the current programme to reduce chain migration.
“This new application process benefits applicants who can speak English, have financial support, and have skills that are beneficial to the development of the economy.”
