Does meat, dairy, and chocolate help to relieve inflammatory bowel disease (IBD)?
Cute meat and chocolate may sound like a nightmare for your digestive system.
But a new study suggests the opposite: A diet rich in meat protein and dairy products can help alleviate symptoms associated with inflammatory bowel disease patients.
It affects about 1.3 million Americans and about 300,000 Britons, resulting in stomach cramps and bloating, recurrent or haemorrhagic diarrhoea, weight loss and extreme tiredness.
Researchers at the University of Washington usually advise patients to avoid eating meat and dairy products to relieve symptoms, but the researchers have found that the protein’s key amino acid, tryptophan, can help promote the growth of immune cells, and these cells can improve the tolerance of the intestine.
Lead researcher Dr. Marco Colonna explained that immune cells patrol the gut to make sure harmful microbes hidden in food don’t crept into the body.
Maintain a balance between the inflammatory cells and those that enhance tolerance, protecting the body without harming a wide range of sensitive and vulnerable tissues.
Inflammatory bowel disease can occur when the equilibrium state is too biased towards inflammation.
In the experiment, it was found that an immune-promoting cell appeared in mice that carried special bacteria.
Bacteria require tryptophan (one of the components of the protein) to form the appearance of the cells.
Professor Colonna said: “We established a link between a bacteriological population ( Lactobacillus remycosis, which is a normal part of the gut microbiota) and cell population development that promotes tolerance.
The more tryptophan the mice consumed in their diet, the more immune cells they had.
He suggests that if humans use the same approach, i.e. a combination of Lactobacillus and tryptophan-rich diets may form a more tolerable and less inflammatory gut environment.
Luisa Cervantes-Barraganwas, a postdoctoral researcher, studied a type of immune cell that enhances tolerability, when she found that one group of mice studied had such cells, but the other group of the same strains were raised separately.
She suspects that this difference is associated with a community of gut microbes (referring to bacteria, viruses, and fungi that typically live in the gastrointestinal tract).
DNA sequencing of the mice’s cholesterol and found that there were six bacterial populations present in mice with immune cells, but none in mice without immune cells.
The mice were raised in a sterile environment, so they lacked gut microbes and were unable to develop such immune cells, while the presence of Lactobacillus produced immune cells.
In order to understand how the bacterium affects the immune system, the researchers cultured Lactobacillus in the liquid and then transferred a small amount of bacteria-free liquid to immature immune cells isolated from the mice.
These immune cells develop into tolerant cells.
When purifies the active ingredient from the liquid, it can be shown that the active ingredient is a by-product of tryptophan metabolism, known as indole-3 lactic acid.
When the researchers doubled the amount of tryptophan in rat feed, the number of such cells increased by about 50 percent, but when tryptophan levels were halved, the number of cells was cut in half.
Cervantes-Barragan, Dr. Cervantes-Barragan, explained that people, like mice, have the same tolerance-enhancing cells, and most of us have Lactobacillus in our gastrointestinal tract.
It has not yet been known whether humans, like mice in an experiment, can induced cell development in the body's tryptophan by-products from Lactobacillus, but gene defects related to tryptophan have been found in patients with inflammatory bowel disease.
She said: "The development of these cells may be exactly what we want, because these cells can control the inflammatory response on the internal surface of the intestine."
It may be inaccurate to say that the high levels of tryptophan present in Lactobacillus may lead to an increase in the number of this species.
Jose-Mournoum believes Manchester United have signed 'genius' Nemanja Matic
On Wednesday night, after Nemanja Matic’s debut in the Sampdoria match, Mourinho identified Manchester United signing a “genius” midfielder.
Matic, who came from Chelsea with a £40 million signing, opened 2-1 in his final pre-season game before the European Super Cup in Dublin against Real Madrid on Tuesday, winning the favor of Paul Pogba and Andreas Pereira.
However, Matildiītč was seriously under-matched on the Blues pre-season Asian tour, finishing only 45 minutes and Mourinho admitted that improvements were needed before the start of the Premier League season.
“He needs time, but he’s got the experience, the intelligence and the way of the genius – he thinks about football,” Mourinho said.
“We’re going to get him ready as soon as possible.”
At the beginning of the season, Mourinho began arranging his starting line-up at the beginning of the season. Like Matic, new signings Victor Lindelof and Romelu Lukaku have also started matches at the Aviva Stadium.
The Independent reported this week that Mourinho is still hoping to bring in three more signings, but he insists that the club "does a great job" and that he has four preferred signings in his heart, and the club has brought in three of them.
“I’m very grateful that the club brought in three of the signatories,” he added.
“I’d be happier if the club could bring in all four players, but they’ve done a lot for me.”
The world is climaxing the frigate China if it does not build this type of warship will fall behind?
Recently, the world's major naval powers have announced plans for the construction of new frigates, as if overnight the frigate has become the focus of the attention of the major powerful navies, first Japan in the 2018 annual defense budget to determine the procurement of two new frigates, so that Japan's DEX frigate program has finally achieved a substantial breakthrough, and then the United States Lockheed Martin recently announced the U.S. FFG frigate plan of the latest plan.
At the end of 2017, with the launch of the latest 054A frigate at the end of 2017, it marks that the 054A frigate has built up to 29 ships, which has been approaching the sum of the 053H series frigates, and since the first 054A was launched in 2006, the 054A has been built for more than 12 years.
The reason to build so many 054A is also very simple, it is affordable, easy to use, and supplement the Navy owes for many years.
The 054A frigate has been favored by the Chinese Navy for many years with a high cost performance and a good fighting force, its displacement of about 4000 tons, equipped with a 76 mm main gun, 32-unit sea red flag -16 and fish-8 anti-submarine missile a common launch of the vertical hair system, 8 eagle strikes 83 and a straight-9 helicopter, although it was built in 2006, the design time is a very early type of a ship, but its combat power is not too bad, looking at the world.
However, after all, it is a ship designed at the beginning of the 21st century, the weapon configuration is set aside, its power system and electronic radar equipment compared with the world's mainstream frigates already have a big gap, such as the same type of frigate in Europe has been equipped with all-electric propulsion, small multi-functional phased array radar, large-size helicopter deck.
So how China's new frigate should develop is directly related to its future positioning and the strategic approach of our Chinese navy.
The future development of China's navy will surely become a blue-water navy, and in the future it will certainly go to the ocean, with the rapid deployment of areas where China's vital interests are closely related, demonstrate the existence of force, and can have a strong fighting force if necessary to ensure that China's vital interests in the region are not damaged.
Looking at the positioning problem of new frigates in the future Chinese naval sequence, the future Chinese Navy should be similar to the U.S. Navy, in addition to the necessary offshore defense ships, the other main ships will form an aircraft carrier strike group or amphibious assault ship strike group according to the needs of the situation.
The role of the new frigate in the future aircraft carrier battle group should serve as an anti-submarine main force and the positioning of the mid-to-navigation, in the amphibious assault ship strike group should serve as a frigate class, then according to such a demand, the new frigate must have a strong anti-submarine capability and a good medium-range area clearance capability.
Based on the above positioning, we can boldly imagine the general appearance of domestic frigates in the future.
First of all, the displacement relative to the current 054A frigate will have a substantial increase, it is estimated that the displacement of the new frigate will reach about 5000-6000 tons; the power system will use a QC280 improved gas turbine and two diesel engines composed of an integrated electric propulsion system, the highest speed is expected to reach about 30 knots, the endurance will also be greatly increased; as for the weapon configuration of 76 mm main guns and 1130 close defense guns should also be retained, but will add a red flag 10 firing system.
In this way, the overall level of the new frigate will reach the current first-class level in the world, even compared with the FFG in the United States.
Of course, the above-mentioned concept is only the author's conjecturation for domestic new frigates, how we can only wait until the new frigate is launched to find out, let's look forward to it together.
( Makarov)
(Compilation/Feng Xue)
