From 2005 to 2011, our province's GDP rose from the middle to the "bottom".
However, there are still difficulties such as low investment efficiency and the lack of core competitiveness of the industrial economy in the province's economic growth. To this end, the latest issue of the "Economic Blue Page" of the provincial economic information center proposes to improve the quality and efficiency of economic growth.
Based on some representative indicators of the province's economy in 2005 and 2011, it will be compared with the national and central regions.
In terms of industrial and economic benefits, in 2011, a considerable proportion of high-energy-consuming industries such as industrial energy and raw materials in our province were greatly affected by market fluctuations and "dual pressure" of overcapacity; at the same time, leading industries such as home appliances and automobiles had insufficient innovation, resulting in meager profits.
A large amount of investment does not bring corresponding economic benefits, which is an important reason for the low quality and efficiency of economic growth in our province.
In this regard, the experts suggest that effective measures should be taken to encourage enterprise innovation, and the scientific and technological achievements of universities and research institutes should also be transferred to enterprises in a timely manner.
For industrial economic efficiency is not very high, experts say that we should also actively promote industrial mergers and acquisitions, optimize the industrial layout, and extend the industrial chain.
