News on January 3: The reporter was informed yesterday from the Guangzhou Flower Market Office that the 2008 Yingchun Flower City will start bidding in the near future.
On the 29th and 30th of last month, Huadu District made bids for orange and flower positions respectively.
The Yuexiu District Archives is organizing and collecting hundreds of old photos of the historic Yingchun Flower City (the filming date is 50 or 60 years old), and is scheduled to hold a public exhibition at the Yuexiu District Cultural and Art Center on January 8, 2008, and when the construction of the flower market begins at the end of January, these old photos will be moved to the Beijing Road Guangbai Square for the exhibition.
In addition, the Yuexiu District Culture Bureau will also hold a flower market forum, inviting Guangzhou's old leaders, social folklore experts, social celebrities, the old neighborhoods of Beijing Road to talk about the history and future development of Beijing Road West Lake.
At that time, the flower market forum will contact the online media to carry out online live broadcasting and interact with the public simultaneously.
In addition, it has also opened an online flower market, using the community information network to send text messages to the citizens who enter the Beijing road business district and the West Lake Road Flower Market, and can use the mobile phone to browse the "online flower market".
