LONDON, Jan. 9 (Xinhua) -- The British Sports Council on the 9th announced its goal to participate next month's Pyeongchang Winter Olympics in South Korea: to win at least five medals, which is the "most ambitious" goal of the British delegation in the history of the Olympic Winter Games.
The British sports board is responsible for the allocation of funds for each Olympic project, of course, it is also responsible for issuing the winning targets for each project.
It is estimated that British athletes have the potential to impact medals from snowboarding, curling, steel frame snowmobiles and short track speed skating and so on.
In the past Winter Olympic cycle, the British Sports Council has allocated a total of 32 million pounds (about 280 million yuan) of training funds for the Olympic Winter Games project, and the cycle has doubled.
Most of this money comes from the National Lottery, and the rest comes from state finances.
Britain's hopes of winning gold are mainly placed on two people, one is Alice Christie, the world short track speed skating champion of last year's world short track speed skating, and the other is the previous women's steel frame snowmobile champion Liz Arnold.
At the 2014 Sochi Winter Olympic Games, the British delegation achieved a record of 1 gold, 1 silver and 2 copper, which is the best record they have achieved since the first Winter Olympic Games in 1924.
